    "summary": "ScaffCC is a quantum computing compiler framework built on a modified LLVM/Clang infrastructure. The architecture has three major layers: (1) a quantum programming layer consisting of Scaffold language algorithm implementations and a reusable quantum gate library, (2) a full compiler toolchain based on a heavily modified Clang frontend that parses Scaffold programs through a standard lexer→parser→AST→codegen pipeline generating LLVM IR, with all the supporting infrastructure of diagnostics, serialization, static analysis, and tooling, and (3) quantum-specific post-processing tools including gridsynth for rotation gate synthesis and BraidFlash for fault-tolerant topological quantum compilation. The compiler core follows classic compiler architecture with clear separation between basic infrastructure, AST representation, frontend parsing/semantic analysis, and backend code generation, while the quantum algorithms serve as both benchmarks and example programs for the framework."
